---

<CaseStudyLayout
  title="MMA Class Tracker"
  description="A web app that gamifies showing up to martial arts class: experience points, level-ups and new characters, synced across devices."
  client="Side project"
  role="Design & development"
  year="2023"
  pageTitle="MMA Class Tracker side project | Manny Pachano"
  slides={[
    {
      title: 'The app',
      src: '/videos/web-development-project-mma.mp4',
      poster: '/images/mma.svg',
    },
  ]}
  highlights={[
    { value: 'EXP per class', label: 'Harder classes earn more points' },
    { value: 'Level-ups', label: 'Animated progress bars and new characters' },
    { value: 'Cross-device', label: 'Progress stored in Firebase, works on any screen' },
  ]}
  overview={[
    'My friends and I needed a reason to stop skipping martial arts class. So I built one: <strong>a tracker that turns attendance into a game.</strong> Every class you attend earns experience points, tougher classes earn more, and as the bar fills you level up and unlock a new character.',
    'The front end is hand-written HTML, CSS and JavaScript, with animated progress bars that react the moment a class is logged. Google Firebase stores everyone\'s progress so the app stays in sync between phones and laptops. It is fully responsive, which was half the point: this project was a deliberate workout in responsive design.',
    'It is a small app, but it did its job. We showed up more, and I got a cleaner mental model for state, sync and motion that I still use on client work.',
  ]}
  tools={['HTML & CSS', 'JavaScript', 'Google Firebase', 'GitHub', 'Netlify']}
/>
